Patch 2049: GPU vertex pulling for draws whose attributes come from up to 4 separate streams (VPULL_MULTI=0 off).

In J-Stars' demo fights about 20% of indexed draws fell back to the CPU path on "layout" (attributes in more than one
stream: different strides or buffers), and read_vp_vertex_fast was still 12.5% of the drawing thread. The pulling
shader already reads each attribute with its own offset and stride (vpull_attr); only the copy into the ring assumed
one interleaved stream. A several-stream call now gets one record of its own, one region per stream, and each
attribute's offset points into its stream's region; such a record is not extended by later calls.

Tested (US disc, bench.ps1): pulled 99% of indexed draws (was ~79%); demo 20.14 / 20.56 / 20.51 flips/s (median
20.51) against the fix baseline 18.61 / 18.67 / 19.34 (median 18.67), all three above its best; Free Battle 19.84
against 20.68 (the route's fight varies); pictures right (bench\exp\2026-11-07_1555-vpullmulti).

